my character is level 20, that +20 exactly cancels the -20 armor
penalty.

Now, add in the luck bonus (+13) and the strength and dexterity bonuses
(+6) and that means that -- on this 20 sided die roll -- any number I
throw is going to have 19 added to it, So I'm practically guaranteed to
hit anything with armor class 0 or higher, which is most monsters.  And
I haven't even factored in the skill bonuses or the weapon enchantment.


Bottom line:  I agree with Andrew. If you are of high level AND have
maxed out your luck, a -7 penalty is of no concern.   If -20 won't stop
me,  -7 won't stop you. 

